      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels like it's all just math at the end of the day. if there's no inherent meaning in the universe, then there's no objective difference between existing and not existing. they both just equal zero. so if the value is the same, why is one considered \"better\" than the other? it feels like people just pretend there's a reason to stay because they're afraid of the nothingness.",
